From: Matt
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: mmcc-msm8994: keep MDSS GDSC on (bootloader DSI PLL)

Bring-up hack, not for upstream as is: the DSI PLLs live in the MDSS power
domain and there is no 20nm DSI PLL driver, so the display relies on the
bootloader having set the PLL up. Turning the domain off during probe loses
that setup and the byte clock RCG can no longer switch (-EBUSY).

---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8994.c	2026-10-25 14:50:30.015854095 +0100
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8994.c	2026-10-25 14:50:30.029907746 +0100
@@ -2304,6 +2304,12 @@
 		.name = "mdss_gdsc",
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	/*
+	 * The DSI PLLs sit in this power domain and mainline has no 20nm DSI
+	 * PLL driver: keep the domain up so the bootloader's PLL setup
+	 * survives the display driver's probe (OnePlus 2 bring-up).
+	 */
+	.flags = ALWAYS_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc camss_top_gdsc = {
